{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 7, :comments ["<b>And he made himself strange to them.</b> As soon as he saw them he recognized them immediately, and feared lest they recognize him. Therefore he made himself strange to them, for the mitre was on his head and part of his face, and he altered himself — in the manner of what is said concerning the wife of Jeroboam (1 Kings 14): ״קומי נא והשתנית״ — 'Arise, I pray you, and disguise yourself' — and ״ולא ידעו כי את אשת ירבעם״ — 'and they did not know that she was the wife of Jeroboam'; and it is written concerning the wife of Jeroboam (ibid.): ״למה זה את מתנכרה״ — 'Why do you make yourself strange?' Or he made himself strange to them in words and spoke harshly to them, and said to them in anger, as though no man comes before him to buy grain: 'From where do you come before me?' And they said: 'From the land of Canaan to buy food.' And when they mentioned this, it became clear to him that they were truly his brothers, and this is the meaning of the further statement ״ויכר יוסף את אחיו״ — 'And Joseph recognized his brothers' — for there was added to him recognition and true knowledge of them. Thus explained the Ramban, of blessed memory." "<b>And in the Midrash:</b> ״ויתנכר אליהם״ — he made himself a stranger to them. He took the goblet and struck it, and said to them: 'I see in the goblet that you are spies.' They said to him: 'We are honest men, but our father commanded us not to enter through one gate.' He said to them: 'In the market of harlots, what is your business?' They said to him: 'A lost object is lost to us, and we were searching for it — it has been lost today three days.' He said to them: 'I see in my goblet that two of you destroyed a great city of Shechem.' Immediately they all trembled and said to him: ״שנים עשר עבדיך אחים אנחנו״ — 'Your servants are twelve brothers.' He said to them: 'Where are the two?' They said to him: ״האחד איננו והקטן את אבינו היום״ — 'One is no more, and the youngest is today with our father.' He said to them: ״הביאו אחיכם הקטן אלי ואדעה כי לא מרגלים אתם כי כנים אתם״ — 'Bring your youngest brother to me, and I shall know that you are not spies, for you are honest.'"], :book :genesis, :voice :rabbeinu-bahya, :lang :en, :chapter 42, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T14:19:51.727480076Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}